# Differential cases of jq's math builtins: a C library function on the doubles of numbers. Format:
# oracle/src/main/java/dev/rail8/jq/oracle/diff/DiffCase.java. Expected outputs live in the .rec of the same name,
# written by scripts/oracle-record.sh only. Ids are immutable. Every case uses -c and stdin null; -0 is written
# 0*-1, since the literal -0 is +0, and a NaN prints as null, so a case that shows signs maps each result r to
# copysign(1; r): the sign of a zero, an infinity and a NaN.

# The computed functions on their edges: zeros, ones, subnormals, the largest, infinities and NaN.
# A case whose last digits differ from jq's pins DEVIATIONS.md "libm last digits": its engine-stdout holds this
# engine's digits, which the bound test measures against jq's.

case math-computed/acos-edges
arg -c
filter [0, 0*-1, 1, -1, 0.5, -0.5, 2, -2, 5e-324, -5e-324, 2.225073858507201e-308, 2.2250738585072014e-308, 1e-300, 1e300, -1e300, 1.7976931348623157e308, -1.7976931348623157e308, infinite, -infinite, nan, -nan] | map(acos)
stdin null\n
end

